-- Doc 03 §6.5 published `[first, ...rest] = values`. Doc 18 §7 then removed
-- `...` from the language, and both of Rust's own tokens were already
-- Redox's: `..` to discard and `rest @ ..` to bind.
--
-- An author who writes this followed a published specification, so the
-- message names the correction rather than the token — the same reason
-- `RDX0106` exists for doc 01 §4.3's module-scope binding.
main : ()
main =
  [first, ...rest] = values
  println! \-> "#{first}"
